---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const SPEC = 'https://github.com/RobotRegistryFoundation/rcan-spec/blob/master/spec/appendix-c-physical-assurance.md';
const ENVELOPE_SCHEMA = 'https://rcan.dev/schemas/envelope.json';
const GATE_SCHEMA = 'https://rcan.dev/schemas/gate-decision.json';
const TESTS = 'https://github.com/RobotRegistryFoundation/rcan-spec/blob/master/tests/assurance/README.md';

const requirements = [
  { id: 'R1', title: 'Declared envelope', plain: 'The robot publishes its limits in a machine-readable file: where it may go, how fast, how hard it may push, and how quickly and how far it takes to stop.', test: 'Measure the machine from outside. Nothing measured may exceed what was declared.' },
  { id: 'R2', title: 'Enforcement below the model', plain: 'A small gate between the AI model and the motors checks every command. The model cannot change the gate, the limits or the log.', test: 'Replace the model with a program that sends random and extreme commands. The machine must never leave its envelope.' },
  { id: 'R3', title: 'Stop always wins', plain: 'Every authorised stop overrides everything else within a declared time. If power, communications or a heartbeat is lost, the machine goes to a safe state.', test: 'At top speed, trigger each stop source and measure time and distance to standstill.' },
  { id: 'R4', title: 'Accountable commands', plain: 'Every command that moves the machine can be traced to the person or system that authorised it.', test: 'Audit the log: no executed command without an authorising principal.' },
  { id: 'R5', title: 'Tamper-evident evidence', plain: 'Every gate decision (allow, clamp, reject, stop) is written to an append-only, hash-chained log.', test: 'Verify the chain and replay each decision against the declared envelope.' },
];

const levels = [
  { id: 'A1', name: 'Declared', desc: 'Published envelope, gate in a separate process from the model, hash-chained log.' },
  { id: 'A2', name: 'Enforced', desc: 'A1 plus: gate on independent compute or firmware, a hardware stop path, heartbeat watchdogs, and passing the fault-injection tests.' },
  { id: 'A3', name: 'Assured', desc: 'A2 plus: gate and stop path meet a functional-safety integrity target (ISO 13849 PL or IEC 61508 SIL) with third-party testing.' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Physical Assurance — Robot Registry Foundation"
  description="How the registry records a robot's physical assurance level: the model proposes, a bounded layer disposes. Self-declared levels A1–A2, A3 only with third-party evidence."
>
  <div class="pt-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-text-muted font-mono mb-8">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent transition-colors">RRF</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="text-text">Physical assurance</span>
    </div>

    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold text-text mb-4">Physical assurance</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-text-muted mb-6 leading-relaxed">
      The model proposes; a bounded layer disposes.
    </p>

    <div class="p-5 bg-bg-card border border-border rounded-xl mb-12 text-sm text-text-muted space-y-2">
      <p><strong class="text-text">Conformance is not certification.</strong> <strong class="text-text">Compliance evidence is not regulatory sufficiency.</strong> What the registry holds is evidence a robot's owner chose to publish.</p>
      <p>RCAN and this registry have one maintainer and no third-party verification. The registry does not test robots and does not review linked evidence.</p>
      <p>To be presented at the ITU-T FG-EAI workshop on embodied AI, 16 October 2026 (remote). That is a presentation, not an endorsement by ITU or anyone else.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-text mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-border">The idea</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Any AI model may propose what a robot does next. A small, deterministic gate between the model and the
          motors decides what actually runs. The safety claim rests on the gate, which can be tested without the
          model's weights, rather than on the model, which cannot be tested exhaustively.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is not new. It is the Simplex architecture (Sha, 2001) and the run-time assurance pattern standardised
          for aircraft in ASTM F3269. What RCAN adds is a vendor-neutral <em>test method</em> for machines driven by
          learned policies: five requirements, each with a pass/fail test a third party can run.
        </p>
        <p>
          It complements, and replaces none of, ISO 10218, ISO/TS 15066, ISO 13482, IEC 60204-1, ISO 13849,
          IEC 61508 and ITU-T F.748.44. F.748.44 benchmarks the model; this tests the machine around it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-text mb-6 pb-2 border-b border-border">Five requirements</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        {requirements.map(r => (
          <div class="p-5 bg-bg-card border border-border rounded-xl">
            <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3 mb-2">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">{r.id}</span>
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-text">{r.title}</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-2">{r.plain}</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-text-faint leading-relaxed"><span class="font-mono">Test:</span> {r.test}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-muted mt-4">
        The gate makes one of four decisions for every command: <span class="font-mono">allow</span>,
        <span class="font-mono">clamp</span>, <span class="font-mono">reject</span> or <span class="font-mono">stop</span>.
        If anything goes wrong inside the gate (an error, a timeout, stale sensor data, a command it cannot read) the
        answer is <span class="font-mono">stop</span>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-text mb-6 pb-2 border-b border-border">Assurance levels</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-4 mb-6">
        {levels.map(l => (
          <div class="flex gap-4 p-5 bg-bg-card border border-border rounded-xl">
            <span class="font-mono text-lg text-accent shrink-0">{l.id}</span>
            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold text-text mb-1">{l.name}</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed">{l.desc}</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="p-5 bg-primary/8 border border-primary/20 rounded-xl text-sm text-text leading-relaxed">
        Assurance levels A1–A3 are a separate axis from RCAN's protocol conformance levels L1–L4. An L-level says how
        well a robot speaks the protocol; an A-level says how well its motion is bounded.
        <strong>An RCAN L3 robot can be A1.</strong>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-text mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-border">Two different stops</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="p-5 bg-bg-card border border-border rounded-xl">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-text mb-2">RCAN ESTOP message</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed">Fast, authenticated, honoured from any principal, and logged. It depends on software being alive to receive it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 bg-bg-card border border-border rounded-xl">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-text mb-2">Hardwired power cut</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed">A circuit that removes actuator power without going through the gate, the model or the runtime. It works when software is the failure.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-muted mt-4">Both are needed. They are not the same thing, and a robot with only one of them does not have the other.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-text mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-border">What the registry shows</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-accent">→</span> A robot record may carry <span class="font-mono">assurance_level</span>, <span class="font-mono">envelope_hash</span> and <span class="font-mono">assurance_evidence_url</span>, supplied by its owner.</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-accent">→</span> A1 and A2 are always labelled <em>self-declared</em>.</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-accent">→</span> A3 is shown only when a third-party evidence link is present. The registry links to that evidence; it does not review it.</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-accent">→</span> A safety-benchmark submission may list which EV tests (EV-01 to EV-09) it covers. That list is shown as self-reported.</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-accent">→</span> No registry endpoint accepts test results as verified.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-text mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-border">Out of scope</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        Whether the declared limits are right for a task or a site; harm the machine can do while staying inside its
        limits; how well the machine senses people; general cybersecurity; and identity and delegation mechanics
        (the subject of ITU FG-TIDA).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-text mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-border">Read the spec</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li><a href={SPEC} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent hover:underline">RCAN Appendix C: Physical Assurance Profile →</a></li>
        <li><a href={ENVELOPE_SCHEMA} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent hover:underline">Envelope schema (envelope.json) →</a></li>
        <li><a href={GATE_SCHEMA} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent hover:underline">Gate decision record schema (gate-decision.json) →</a></li>
        <li><a href={TESTS} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent hover:underline">EV-01 to EV-09 test plan and status →</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
